WEBVTT

00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:01.680
Good evening everyone.

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:06.809
It is Thursday, June 25th, 2026, 5:30 p.m.,

00:01:06.849 --> 00:01:10.250
and this session of the Huntsville City Council is called to order.

00:01:10.330 --> 00:01:12.739
We are met in the chambers in Huntsville,

00:01:12.809 --> 00:01:13.529
Alabama.

00:01:13.930 --> 00:01:18.730
We welcome all those who have joined us here tonight in person and many

00:01:18.730 --> 00:01:22.510
who are joining us virtually on several streaming platforms.

00:01:23.000 --> 00:01:26.830
We will begin our meeting tonight as is our practice with an invocation

00:01:26.830 --> 00:01:30.389
offered by one of our Huntsville, Alabama police safety chaplains,

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:34.580
Chaplain Don Eadie, which will be followed by the Pledge of Allegiance given

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.419
by council member John Meredith.

00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:41.120
All who wish to do so are able, please stand for the invocation and pledge

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:41.980
of allegiance.

00:01:46.709 --> 00:01:50.269
Father, we come before you today at the close of this day just grateful

00:01:50.269 --> 00:01:52.040
for your gifts to us today.

00:01:52.940 --> 00:01:56.349
Thank you for the gift of life, for the ability to interact,

00:01:56.860 --> 00:02:00.900
to laugh, uh, Lord, to have conversations,

00:02:01.110 --> 00:02:05.790
to understand one another, and we're just grateful for this thing that we

00:02:05.790 --> 00:02:07.629
call life, and we wanna thank you.

00:02:08.309 --> 00:02:12.149
We thank you for the lives of the little ones here in our city,

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.809
for those who have just been born this past week,

00:02:15.270 --> 00:02:20.020
this past month, for the children, we're grateful and we take that as a

00:02:20.020 --> 00:02:24.869
stewardship upon them and Lord, thank you for the gift of these little ones.

00:02:25.710 --> 00:02:29.490
Lord, we pray for the council members tonight that you give them discernment

00:02:29.500 --> 00:02:33.279
and discretion as they work through the issues they have of the evening.

00:02:33.710 --> 00:02:37.509
We pray for the public who's gathered here that you would give them grace

00:02:37.509 --> 00:02:40.570
and understanding as, uh, the two work together.

00:02:41.130 --> 00:02:44.350
Lord we just wanna say that we love you and we pray that you would help

00:02:44.350 --> 00:02:48.669
us to love you and to love one another as we love ourselves,

00:02:48.869 --> 00:02:51.369
and we pray this in the name of the Lord Jesus.

00:02:51.789 --> 00:02:52.270
Amen.

00:02:57.149 --> 00:03:02.759
Allegiance to the flag of the United States of America and to the republic

00:03:02.919 --> 00:03:06.130
for which it stands, one nation under God,

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.240
indivisible, with liberty and justice for all.

00:03:13.080 --> 00:03:15.779
Thank you, Chaplain Eadie, and thank you,

00:03:15.889 --> 00:03:17.000
Council Member Meredith.

00:03:18.059 --> 00:03:20.119
Council members, we have the agenda.

00:03:20.699 --> 00:03:26.500
Please note that items 19B and 21G have been withdrawn by the sponsor.

00:03:26.860 --> 00:03:30.419
