00:09:11.979 --> 00:09:17.229
Item 6A is a resolution recognizing the remarkable life and legacy of Representative

00:09:17.229 --> 00:09:19.549
James Howard Sanderford.

00:09:19.700 --> 00:09:22.510
Is there a motion to motion to approve motion from Mr.

00:09:22.630 --> 00:09:22.989
Little.

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:24.299
Second from the chair.

00:09:24.349 --> 00:09:26.419
All in favor, please indicate opposed.

00:09:26.510 --> 00:09:27.340
The motion carries.

00:09:27.549 --> 00:09:27.710
Mr.

00:09:27.789 --> 00:09:31.450
Kling, would you like to join me in, uh, presenting the resolution?

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:43.820
We have Mr.

00:09:43.830 --> 00:09:45.789
Sanderford's family here.

00:09:45.869 --> 00:09:47.989
Would you like to come and join us up here?

00:09:48.750 --> 00:09:52.580
Uh, we have his one of his 3 daughters, Peggy is with us,

00:09:52.679 --> 00:09:55.039
2 grandchildren, and I will, while they're coming up,

00:09:55.119 --> 00:10:00.000
I'll tell you that at the visitation when in January when we suggested to

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:02.190
the family that we would like to do a resolution,

00:10:02.599 --> 00:10:04.559
they said we will all, they're all from out of town.

00:10:04.640 --> 00:10:09.599
We will all be back in June for a wedding which has taken place and so now

00:10:09.599 --> 00:10:14.520
we are able to present the resolution in Representative Sanderford's honor.

00:10:16.570 --> 00:10:19.330
Whereas the city council and the mayor of the city of Huntsville,

00:10:19.359 --> 00:10:22.690
Alabama wish to recognize the remarkable life and legacy of Representative

00:10:22.690 --> 00:10:26.530
James Howard Sanderford, who will long be remembered for his innovative

00:10:26.530 --> 00:10:29.530
entrepreneurship, unwavering service to his country,

00:10:29.809 --> 00:10:32.109
and steadfast leadership in the community.

00:10:33.280 --> 00:10:37.039
He had a dedicated following a dedicated military service,

00:10:37.280 --> 00:10:41.510
Sanderford built a distinguished professional career with IBM from which

00:10:41.510 --> 00:10:44.950
he later retired before founding computer company Leasing Inc.

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:48.359
demonstrating his entrepreneurial spirit and lasting contributions to the

00:10:48.359 --> 00:10:48.679
business.

00:10:48.780 --> 00:10:53.260
Community, he was elected to the Alabama House of Representatives in 1989

00:10:53.260 --> 00:10:58.299
in a special election representing Alabama's 20th district and served there

00:10:58.299 --> 00:11:02.700
until 2022 believing that serving the citizens of Huntsville and Madison

00:11:02.700 --> 00:11:04.419
County was the honor of a lifetime.

00:11:05.229 --> 00:11:07.909
He was definitely a public servant.

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.950
Representative Sanderford served in various leadership roles,

00:11:11.150 --> 00:11:14.429
including co-chair of the Joint Legislative Sunset Committee,

00:11:14.750 --> 00:11:17.140
chair of the House Boards, agencies and commissions Committee,

00:11:17.219 --> 00:11:20.510
and chair of the Alabama Legislative Medal of Honor for Law Enforcement.

00:11:20.789 --> 00:11:25.070
He was very proud of his service in that capacity as an active leader in

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:29.289
his community, he served on the US, uh, Space and Rocket Center board.

00:11:30.359 --> 00:11:33.809
I was past president of the Huntsville Rotary and someone just told me that

00:11:33.809 --> 00:11:36.789
half of the members of Rotary were recruited by Howard,

00:11:37.130 --> 00:11:37.969
um, his path.

00:11:40.559 --> 00:11:43.960
Past chair of the Madison County Republican Executive Committee and past

00:11:43.960 --> 00:11:46.989
co-chair of the Chamber of Commerce Free Enterprise Committee,

00:11:47.119 --> 00:11:49.690
reflecting his dedication to the betterment of the city of Huntsville,

00:11:50.159 --> 00:11:52.159
he was also an active member of his church,

00:11:52.349 --> 00:11:54.950
First Baptist Church, where he served as a deacon,

00:11:55.039 --> 00:11:57.840
finance committee chair, youth Sunday school director and teacher,

00:11:57.919 --> 00:12:00.479
demonstrating exemplary faith and service to Christ.

00:12:00.979 --> 00:12:04.619
And whereas Representative Sanderford not only faithfully served his country,

00:12:04.630 --> 00:12:08.469
community, and church, he was also a dedicated husband to his wife Dot of

00:12:08.469 --> 00:12:11.750
67 years, devoted father to three daughters,

00:12:11.830 --> 00:12:13.989
Mary Anne, Peggy, who's with us tonight.

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:18.229
And Betty and loving grandchildren or loving grandfather to 8 children.

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:21.059
Now therefore be it resolved that the city of,

00:12:21.559 --> 00:12:24.559
uh, that the city council and mayor of the city of Huntsville hereby honor

00:12:24.559 --> 00:12:27.080
the life of Representative James Howard Sanderford,

00:12:27.239 --> 00:12:32.039
recognizing years of faithful service to his country and 3 decades of committed

00:12:32.039 --> 00:12:34.280
leadership in the city of Huntsville and Madison County.

00:12:34.719 --> 00:12:38.109
Due to his prominent influence, Representative James Howard Sanderford's

00:12:38.109 --> 00:12:42.320
legacy and impact will be acknowledged and remembered for generations to

00:12:42.320 --> 00:12:42.640
come.

00:12:45.159 --> 00:12:45.440
his office too.

00:12:46.549 --> 00:12:47.590
Thank you for being with us.

00:12:48.570 --> 00:12:49.890
And thank you each for being here.

00:12:49.979 --> 00:12:50.919
Would you like to introduce your?

00:12:52.169 --> 00:12:54.890
OK, I want to thank you all for this.

00:12:55.010 --> 00:12:57.830
Anybody that knows my dad knows he loved good resolution,

00:12:58.250 --> 00:13:01.840
and so thank you for this and thank you for remembering him.

00:13:02.130 --> 00:13:06.250
He and my mom moved here 50 years ago and made Huntsville their home,

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:10.369
and they loved Huntsville and loved the opportunity to serve here.

00:13:10.489 --> 00:13:12.419
So thank you very much for this.

00:13:12.690 --> 00:13:13.289
Thank you.

00:13:14.630 --> 00:13:18.369
Sure, um, well, let me recognize the ones that aren't here before I,

00:13:18.409 --> 00:13:22.380
um, my older sister Mary Anne and her husband Chip and two sons,

00:13:22.650 --> 00:13:27.530
um, Philip and John and, um, Shannon are not here with us,

00:13:27.570 --> 00:13:32.780
and then my younger sister Betty, who is the mother of Caroline and Grace,

00:13:33.049 --> 00:13:37.989
and Grace is the new wife of Dylan, yeah.

00:13:38.700 --> 00:13:42.070
And this is my husband Morgan, so thank you again very much.

00:13:42.109 --> 00:13:43.679
This is very meaningful to us.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:44.330
Thank you.

00:13:47.679 --> 00:13:48.390
Do you wanna say anything?

00:13:51.349 --> 00:13:55.630
I had, I had the privilege to know Howard both as a fellow elected official

00:13:55.630 --> 00:13:59.250
and also as a news reporter, and he was true blue.

00:13:59.510 --> 00:14:03.450
He cared about the entire city, not just his own legislative district,

00:14:03.750 --> 00:14:06.429
and sometimes there'd be some tough issues out there,

00:14:06.479 --> 00:14:09.169
but he would always return my phone calls and he was a great,

00:14:09.770 --> 00:14:12.510
great person for this community and it was a privilege to have known him.

