00:33:08.199 --> 00:33:08.869
Um, Mr.

00:33:09.000 --> 00:33:11.719
Nunez, would you like to comment on which is more dense,

00:33:11.800 --> 00:33:16.310
1B or 2, or residents 2, and why are we making the change?

00:33:16.359 --> 00:33:17.199
What is the process?

00:33:17.280 --> 00:33:20.599
Yes, so I'll start, um, one with the process itself.

00:33:20.719 --> 00:33:24.719
So, um, upon the city council annexing and zoning property,

00:33:24.800 --> 00:33:27.760
the property is to, uh, have a zoning district that allows.

00:33:27.969 --> 00:33:30.459
For a particular use, uh, through their, uh,

00:33:30.469 --> 00:33:33.109
action, petitioners or property owners, uh,

00:33:33.599 --> 00:33:38.920
perform or perform an application to us to state what their next intended

00:33:38.920 --> 00:33:39.760
uses are.

00:33:40.160 --> 00:33:43.760
Uh, for this development they are changing from a Residence 1B district

00:33:43.760 --> 00:33:45.109
to a residence 2 district.

00:33:45.160 --> 00:33:47.400
The residence 2 district is denser.

00:33:47.739 --> 00:33:51.969
Uh, it is allowable to have a mixture of housing stock,

00:33:52.260 --> 00:33:54.560
um, particularly this development is, uh,

00:33:54.709 --> 00:33:58.930
seeking to petition for a reduction of side yard setbacks.

00:33:59.189 --> 00:34:03.869
Uh, the difference between residence 1B and residence two is approximately

00:34:03.869 --> 00:34:04.979
4 ft on either side.

00:34:05.890 --> 00:34:08.949
Uh, so in residence1B you are to maintain,

00:34:09.090 --> 00:34:11.010
uh, 10 ft on both sides of the home.

00:34:11.090 --> 00:34:14.080
In this case, in residence two, if it is to,

00:34:14.090 --> 00:34:17.040
uh, be approved, then that action would allow for,

00:34:17.050 --> 00:34:19.719
uh, a sum of 16 under residence twoB.

00:34:20.429 --> 00:34:23.290
Furthermore, within the process, the application is received.

00:34:23.409 --> 00:34:25.969
Planning staff reviews that application, uh,

00:34:26.050 --> 00:34:28.870
has deeper discussions with the development teams.

00:34:29.129 --> 00:34:33.409
Uh, at that point, we, uh, send out notification to individuals or property

00:34:33.409 --> 00:34:35.050
owners within 500 ft.

00:34:35.418 --> 00:34:38.520
Those notifications are first heard before planning commission,

00:34:38.610 --> 00:34:42.879
so the entire process takes approximately 9 months and is now,

00:34:43.168 --> 00:34:48.560
so this process started approximately um 75-85 days ago,

00:34:48.969 --> 00:34:52.120
uh, and now it is here before you for this particular,

00:34:52.129 --> 00:34:53.570
uh, action to review.

00:34:55.467 --> 00:34:59.148
Sometimes a denser property results in more affordable housing.

00:34:59.239 --> 00:35:00.519
Would that be the case with this?

00:35:00.638 --> 00:35:01.668
That is also the case.

00:35:01.749 --> 00:35:06.858
Now, overall this development has approximately 350+ acres,

00:35:07.039 --> 00:35:09.239
and there's a mixture of housing styles.

00:35:09.559 --> 00:35:11.158
Uh, in this particular area.

00:35:11.198 --> 00:35:14.878
It is a new growth corridor as we've had a significant amount of growth

00:35:14.878 --> 00:35:15.519
in our.

00:35:15.604 --> 00:35:20.764
Western area, uh, primarily around Mazda Toyota with Amazon and other announcements

00:35:20.764 --> 00:35:23.274
that have come, uh, this is the next, uh,

00:35:23.284 --> 00:35:25.925
growth corridor with new housing development,

00:35:25.965 --> 00:35:30.044
and we wanna put some affordable housing opportunities in this area by creating

00:35:30.044 --> 00:35:31.375
denser developments.

00:35:31.685 --> 00:35:34.985
However, this overall development does have a mixture of,

00:35:35.004 --> 00:35:36.824
uh, housing stock and style.

00:35:37.445 --> 00:35:37.885
Thank you.

