00:59:41.449 --> 00:59:44.449
So, uh, you know council's familiar with,

00:59:44.459 --> 00:59:48.929
uh, the area up on Green Mountain, uh, that's obviously well inside of our

00:59:48.929 --> 00:59:50.969
city but somewhat remote just based on, uh,

00:59:51.050 --> 00:59:52.070
based on the terrain.

00:59:52.330 --> 00:59:54.979
Uh, it does have fire coverage from one of our,

00:59:55.070 --> 00:59:58.050
uh, career fire stations down at the bottom of the mountain,

00:59:58.389 --> 01:00:00.629
uh, but that community for many, many years has also,

01:00:00.929 --> 01:00:04.360
uh, resourced a volunteer fire department that assists with,

01:00:04.370 --> 01:00:06.340
uh, emergency response up on the mountain.

01:00:06.780 --> 01:00:11.750
Uh, in, in recent years, uh, we've worked more closely with them,

01:00:11.870 --> 01:00:14.570
uh, have, uh, have actually provided some real estate,

01:00:15.070 --> 01:00:16.989
uh, well, they really kind of provide it to us and then we,

01:00:17.030 --> 01:00:20.770
uh, we allow them to use the, the small fire station that's up there,

01:00:20.989 --> 01:00:22.969
but also have assisted them with the equipment.

01:00:23.110 --> 01:00:26.169
So one of the trucks that they have right now is one that we actually,

01:00:26.179 --> 01:00:28.919
uh, provided to them out of our, out of our fire department,

01:00:29.350 --> 01:00:30.929
uh, and it's now time to replace that.

01:00:31.350 --> 01:00:33.760
Uh, we think of the arrangement there and then ultimately there,

01:00:33.879 --> 01:00:35.909
there is a point in the future where we will need to,

01:00:35.919 --> 01:00:38.570
uh, build a permanent fire station up on the mountain.

01:00:38.879 --> 01:00:42.280
Uh, so, uh, we've identified the piece of equipment they need.

01:00:42.520 --> 01:00:45.520
They did some fundraising, uh, and now want to donate that money,

01:00:45.600 --> 01:00:49.360
about $110,000 to the city to contribute towards the purchase of the truck

01:00:49.360 --> 01:00:50.080
that they'll use.

01:00:50.520 --> 01:00:54.360
Uh, so ultimately between this and then what we have in our fleet capital

01:00:54.360 --> 01:00:56.919
account already in the capital plan, we will purchase the equipment,

01:00:57.169 --> 01:00:59.879
uh, and then provide that to them to use for emergency response up on the

01:00:59.879 --> 01:01:00.280
mountain.

01:01:00.669 --> 01:01:06.590
And this truck is unique in that it has the capacity to take water far beyond

01:01:06.590 --> 01:01:07.830
what they could get from a hydrant.

01:01:07.939 --> 01:01:10.389
There's, there's really kind of two issues that we have to deal with up

01:01:10.389 --> 01:01:10.949
there on the mountain.

01:01:11.060 --> 01:01:13.300
There's a portion of the development there that are very,

01:01:13.389 --> 01:01:17.909
very large lots, uh, multiple acres, in many cases the houses are well off

01:01:17.909 --> 01:01:19.110
of the public right of way.

01:01:19.489 --> 01:01:21.949
Uh, and so we have to deal with much longer runs of,

01:01:22.090 --> 01:01:25.600
of, uh, lines to get water into the house if there's a fire there.

01:01:26.040 --> 01:01:29.500
Uh, we also have, uh, sometimes in instances of wildland fires there,

01:01:29.600 --> 01:01:33.139
so dealing with, uh, with grass fires and unbrushed fires,

01:01:33.179 --> 01:01:33.659
things like that.

01:01:33.739 --> 01:01:37.260
And so this equipment, uh, is a little bit smaller and actually more maneuverable

01:01:37.260 --> 01:01:40.139
to get into some of those driveways and things over those long distances

01:01:40.139 --> 01:01:41.939
as well as helping with the wildland fire.

01:01:42.530 --> 01:01:46.090
And I should also add for the record that I hope at the next council meeting

01:01:46.090 --> 01:01:51.250
we will see I'm, I'm going to divert $30,000 from my uh council improvement

01:01:51.250 --> 01:01:54.649
fund to fleet to help fund this, um.

