Alabama.

01:16:10.830 --> 01:16:14.410
Uh, first of all, Excuse me, I don't have a prepared,

01:16:14.439 --> 01:16:18.310
uh, presentation, but let me, uh, Uh, acknowledge,

01:16:18.319 --> 01:16:23.069
uh, Council member Michelle Watkins and City Administrator John Hamilton

01:16:23.069 --> 01:16:25.390
for taking the time out of their schedule to,

01:16:25.419 --> 01:16:30.910
uh, hold a meeting on Alabama A&M campus regarding the Black Art Black History

01:16:30.910 --> 01:16:33.020
Museum a couple of weeks ago.

01:16:33.509 --> 01:16:37.569
We appreciate that, uh, several of, uh, community personnel were there,

01:16:38.270 --> 01:16:38.839
uh, Mr.

01:16:38.870 --> 01:16:41.390
William Hampton, uh, Ollie Connolly.

01:16:42.029 --> 01:16:46.680
And, uh, staff from Alabama A&M, thank you all very much for participating

01:16:46.680 --> 01:16:50.140
in the discussion regarding the Black, Black History Museum.

01:16:50.770 --> 01:16:56.299
Now, as we approach 250 years of celebration of American history,

01:16:56.560 --> 01:17:01.660
uh, it would be so nice to have a museum that also acknowledges the contributions

01:17:02.040 --> 01:17:05.500
of minorities, uh, as well as all people,

01:17:05.560 --> 01:17:08.169
uh, that have made Huntsville what it is.

01:17:08.709 --> 01:17:12.339
And uh as we go about celebrating 250 years,

01:17:12.839 --> 01:17:15.450
uh, just coming up here on the 4th of July,

01:17:16.020 --> 01:17:18.959
uh, let's remember all the contributions have been made by people of all

01:17:18.959 --> 01:17:22.990
races, all colors, all nationalities that helped make this country,

01:17:23.000 --> 01:17:26.140
and of course it helped makes Huntsville the city that it is,

01:17:26.439 --> 01:17:30.399
and we're still pushing to have Huntsville recognize a black art,

01:17:30.479 --> 01:17:35.390
black history museum, whether it's on Alabama A&M campus or elsewhere and

01:17:35.390 --> 01:17:37.399
as we read newspaper, magazines.

01:17:37.759 --> 01:17:42.620
Uh, there's very little to nothing that's written about black black art,

01:17:43.160 --> 01:17:46.810
black history here in Huntsville, and we're pushing to get something to,

01:17:47.319 --> 01:17:52.600
to, uh, see, to, uh, be proud about, and to acknowledge the contributions

01:17:52.600 --> 01:17:53.680
made by so many people.

01:17:53.839 --> 01:17:54.200
Thank you.

01:17:55.240 --> 01:17:56.149
